Diseases are very vaguely placed into this category with inconclusive inclusion and exclusion criteria. Following are the basic disease types that fall under this category or one can say they form this category.
Motor Ne[uron] Diseases are characterised[ by] progressive[ muscle] weakness and degeneration of motor[ neuron.] But[ as explained] earlier that classification is vague, so not all motor[ neuron] degeneratory disorders fall under this category and rather they are placed into a broader category called “Motor Ne[uron] Disease Disorders” example Spinal Mus[cular] Atrophies falls into this broader category.
